=== layout: section

# Grading and Assessment

=== layout: one-panel

# Assignments, Quizzes, and Exams

@body

- [*Assignments*]{color=red}: reinforce learning; explore new topics
  - Weekly on Blackboard; 5-15 points; unlimited retakes
  - Collaboration and help encouraged
- [*Quizzes*]{color=red}: recent material
  - Individual: 20 points; 30 minutes
  - Optional group quiz in person during class
- [*Exams*]{color=red}: cumulative midterm and final
  - Individual; 100 points total
  - Each part: 50 points; 75 minutes

=== layout: two-panels

# [*Graded*]{color=#003FFF} vs [*Total*]{color=#C80085} Percentage

@left

- [*Graded percentage*]{color=#003FFF} includes only items with a recorded grade.
- Excludes items that have not been graded, including unfinished assignments.
- More useful when *Dr. Voss* still has submitted work to grade.

@right

- [*Total percentage*]{color=#C80085} includes all items counted toward your Blackboard grade.
- Counts items without a recorded grade as zero.
  - This includes submitted work waiting to be graded.
- More useful for seeing the effect of assignments you have not attempted.

=== layout: section

# Quiz/Exam

=== layout: one-panel

# [Don't Panic]{color=red}

@body

- If you experience internet troubles or non-academic distractions during a quiz/exam\:
  - 1. Don't panic
  - 2. Stop and close the quiz/exam without looking at all the questions
  - 3. [Contact me immediately]{color=red}, preferably via Discord, but you do not need to rush
- Note\: Once class begins, I no longer check my email.
- If you haven't looked at all the questions, I can reset the quiz/exam
- If you have looked at some questions, I can create a new custom quiz/exam with only the portion that you haven't seen yet.

=== layout: one-panel

# Illness Policy

@body

- Since COVID, I am trying to be more considerate of student illnesses.
- If you are sick, let me know. I will provide an extension.
- If a major event interferes (car accident, etc.), again contact me.
- Communication is always helpful.

=== layout: section

# Exam

=== layout: one-panel

# Midterm Next Week: October 13

@body

- Tuesday, Oct 13, 2026: in-person written exam during class
- Chapters 1-4
- Class meeting: 1:30-4:25 p.m.
- Worth 100 points; completed individually
- Review an old exam to see the format

=== layout: two-panels

# In-Person Exam Rules

@left

- Part 1: multiple choice and matching
- ZipGrade bubble answer form
- Variations on assignment and quiz questions
- Questions sorted by lecture
- Fill one bubble completely for each answer

@right

- Part 2: short answers
- Four questions: answer any three; skip one
- Each part: 50 points, 75 minutes

=== layout: one-panel

# What to Bring to the Exam

@body

- Bring a notecard or full sheet of paper as a help sheet
- Dr. Voss provides the Punnett square help sheet
- No electronics or calculators

=== layout: one-panel

# BB Assignments for Mid-Term Exam

@body

- Prepare for the Oct 13 midterm: Chapters 1-4
- Retake available assignments until you understand the questions
- Unlimited homework attempts; only the highest score counts
- Assignments 4-5 are due today, Oct 6
- Assignment 6 is due Oct 13
- Check Blackboard for assignment availability and submission times

